            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "A parallel plate capacitor consists of two circular plates of radius $R=0.1 \\mathrm{~m}$. They are separated by a short distance. If electric field between the capacitor plates changes as $\\frac{d E}{d t}=6 \\times 10^{13} \\frac{\\mathrm{~V}}{\\mathrm{~m} \\times \\mathrm{s}}$, then the value of displacement current is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "ijhBW",
              "text": "15.25 A",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "Kld9N",
              "text": "6.25 A",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "zLKfm",
              "text": "16.67 A",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "C5cOf",
              "text": "4.69 A",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Given, area of plates, $A=\\pi R^2=3.14 \\times(0.1)^2 \\mathrm{~m}^2$ and $\\frac{d E}{d t}=6 \\times 10^{13} \\frac{\\mathrm{~V}}{\\mathrm{~m} \\times \\mathrm{s}}$\nDisplacement current between the plates,\n$\\begin{aligned}\nI_d & =\\varepsilon_0 \\frac{d \\phi}{d t} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad I_d & =\\varepsilon_0 A\\left(\\frac{d E}{d t}\\right) \\quad\\left[\\because \\frac{d \\phi}{d t}=A \\frac{d E}{d t}\\right] \\\\\n& =8.85 \\times 10^{-12} \\times 3.14 \\times(0.1)^2 \\times 6 \\times 10^{13} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad I_d & =16.67 \\mathrm{~A}\n\\end{aligned}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
